    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file `poll_transcription.py` that polls a transcription job and returns the transcript using a concrete external provider, I will choose Amazon Transcribe as the provider. This choice is based on the requirement to use a concrete external provider and make it identifiable in the code. Amazon Transcribe is a widely used service for automatic speech recognition (ASR), and it provides a Python SDK (Boto3) for integration. The code will import the Boto3 library, use the Amazon Transcribe client, and include the service name and region to make the provider identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789854965462,
          "start": 1789854962091
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbab51ab001cHhCmMe0JBAkax",
